---
source: crates/wows-query/tests/dispersion.rs
expression: output
---
ship:
  name: Yamato
  index: PJSB018
  tier: 10
  class: battleship
  nation: Japan
  group: upgradeable
  category: tech_tree
  status: released
  replicas:
    - ARP Yamato
    - Yamato Kai
battery: main_battery
range_km: 15
conclusion: "At 15 km, a 39.2% longer main battery range (26.63 km to 37.07 km with Spotting Aircraft + Gun Fire Control System Modification 2) shrinks vertical dispersion from 120.1 m to 100.6 m; horizontal is unchanged at 192 m. Aiming Systems Modification 1 narrows both: horizontal 192 m to 178.6 m, vertical 120.1 m to 111.7 m."
guns:
  - mount: main battery
    min_radius: 2.8
    ideal_radius: 10
    ideal_distance: 1000
    radius_on_zero: 0.2
    radius_on_delim: 0.6
    radius_on_max: 0.8
    delim: 0.5
builds:
  - build: base
    kind: base
    max_range_km: 26.63
    mounts:
      - mount: main battery
        at_range:
          ellipse:
            horizontal_m: 192
            vertical_m: 120.1
            vertical_ratio: 0.625
  - build: Spotting Aircraft
    kind: range
    max_range_km: 31.96
    max_range_change_pct: 20
    mounts:
      - mount: main battery
        at_range:
          ellipse:
            horizontal_m: 192
            vertical_m: 110.5
            vertical_ratio: 0.576
            horizontal_change_pct: 0
            vertical_change_pct: -8
  - build: Gun Fire Control System Modification 2
    kind: range
    max_range_km: 30.89
    max_range_change_pct: 16
    mounts:
      - mount: main battery
        at_range:
          ellipse:
            horizontal_m: 192
            vertical_m: 113
            vertical_ratio: 0.588
            horizontal_change_pct: 0
            vertical_change_pct: -5.9
  - build: Aiming Systems Modification 1
    kind: accuracy
    max_range_km: 26.63
    max_range_change_pct: 0
    mounts:
      - mount: main battery
        at_range:
          ellipse:
            horizontal_m: 178.6
            vertical_m: 111.7
            vertical_ratio: 0.625
            horizontal_change_pct: -7
            vertical_change_pct: -7
  - build: Main Battery Director System (unique upgrade)
    kind: accuracy
    max_range_km: 26.63
    max_range_change_pct: 0
    mounts:
      - mount: main battery
        at_range:
          ellipse:
            horizontal_m: 178.6
            vertical_m: 111.7
            vertical_ratio: 0.625
            horizontal_change_pct: -7
            vertical_change_pct: -7
  - build: Spotting Aircraft + Gun Fire Control System Modification 2
    kind: range
    max_range_km: 37.07
    max_range_change_pct: 39.2
    mounts:
      - mount: main battery
        at_range:
          ellipse:
            horizontal_m: 192
            vertical_m: 100.6
            vertical_ratio: 0.524
            horizontal_change_pct: 0
            vertical_change_pct: -16.2
  - build: Spotting Aircraft + Gun Fire Control System Modification 2 + Aiming Systems Modification 1
    kind: range_and_accuracy
    max_range_km: 37.07
    max_range_change_pct: 39.2
    mounts:
      - mount: main battery
        at_range:
          ellipse:
            horizontal_m: 178.6
            vertical_m: 93.5
            vertical_ratio: 0.524
            horizontal_change_pct: -7
            vertical_change_pct: -22.1
notes:
  - "horizontal_m = 30 x (minRadius + X_m / 30 x (idealRadius - minRadius) / idealDistance), X_m the firing distance in meters and both radii times the accuracy coefficient (Aiming Systems Modification 1 and the like); it depends only on the firing distance. vertical_m = horizontal_m x vertical_ratio, where vertical_ratio runs linearly from radiusOnZero at 0 km to radiusOnDelim at delim x max range, then to radiusOnMax at max range. A longer max range lowers X / max range, so at the same X the ratio, and with it vertical dispersion, falls whenever radiusOnZero < radiusOnDelim < radiusOnMax. At max range horizontal_m is the port's maximum dispersion."
  - "max range is the modified main battery range: fire control module, upgrades, captain skills and Spotting Aircraft all lengthen it. The game client passes the modified range to the gun, and replay measurements (Colbert at 6 km, 13.8 km against 19.2 km range with range skill and upgrade) showed the predicted 16% smaller vertical spread. Spotting Aircraft lengthens the same range value, so it is assumed to act the same way; that case was not measured."
